10. Key UI Principles

Action first

The first question must be: What requires attention?

Evidence second

Every important risk should be expandable into supporting evidence.

Map as context

The map should support a decision rather than force users to search for one.

Uncertainty visible

Pair risk with confidence/data state.

No color-only semantics

Use texture, icons, labels, and contrast.

Offline transparency

Always show live/cached/stale/offline state.

Responsible automation

AI recommends; authorized people approve where required.

